cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software when using its computational models or implementation. Cite the original research separately."
type: software
title: "Thanks for Nothing: Gratitude, Model Revisability, and the Practice of Realizing Emptiness"
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Daniel Ari
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6232-9096"
version: 0.11.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
repository-code: "https://github.com/docxology/thanks_for_nothing"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A research software package separating source-notebook reconstruction,
  paired GNN-driven synthetic gratitude-inspired recall experiments, and finite
  distinctions among observed absence, missing evidence, counterfactual valuation
  and enacted inquiry toward model revisability. Appreciation for the conditions
  of inquiry motivates a conceptual orientation toward practicing realization of
  emptiness. The finite extension separates preference, costly activity, access,
  exact prior comparison and independent prediction. Computational results do not establish human
  efficacy, clinical benefit or contemplative attainment.
keywords:
  - gratitude
  - active inference
  - generalized notation notation
  - reproducible research
  - counterfactual valuation
  - synthetic experiments
